    <glossary>
    <definition id="def-00001"><term>application</term><meaning>process of translating evidence-based research and ideas into practical solutions to influence and improve human life</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00002"><term>child study movement</term><meaning>social and historical consensus that combined several interests to focus the scientific community’s interest on child development</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00003"><term>human development</term><meaning>scientific perspective that incorporates a multidisciplinary approach to understanding the development process</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00004"><term>lifespan development</term><meaning>scientific study of growth, change and stability in humans from conception until death</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00005"><term>maturation</term><meaning>growth and change in an individual based on underlying biological processes</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00006"><term>psychology</term><meaning>scientific study of the mind and all the behavior it produces</meaning></definition>
    <definition id="def-00007"><term>stability</term><meaning>state in which characteristics and abilities remain the same or function similarly across broad portions of the lifespan</meaning></definition>
    </glossary>
    </document>